<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polonnaruwa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Polonnaruwa is a city in the North Central Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> that served as the island's capital from the 11th to the 13th century. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> ruled from it after taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anuradhapura">Anuradhapura</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayabahu-i">Vijayabahu I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parakramabahu-i">Parakramabahu I</a> kept it as the Sinhalese capital, adorning it with palaces, irrigation tanks and the rock-cut Buddhas of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gal-vihara">Gal Vihara</a>. Its ruins are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa.jpg" alt="Polonnaruwa" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polonnaruwa_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
